# Production Station for Magnetocaloric Material Layered Beds

The invention relates to a production station for producing at least one layered bed—and preferably a plurality of layered beds—of magnetocaloric material. The station comprises a framework, with the following components arranged thereon:

- a material receptacle configured to receive particulate magnetocaloric material;
- a dosing plate having at least one intake opening adapted to receive the magnetocaloric material corresponding to one layer of the layered bed;
- at least one reservoir positioned below the intake opening, the reservoir being adapted to receive one or more layers of the particulate magnetocaloric material.

The production station further comprises a shutter plate arranged between the reservoir and the dosing plate. The shutter plate is switchable via motion relative to the dosing plate and is configured to enable at least a filling mode. In this filling mode, the at least one reservoir is filled with particulate magnetocaloric material corresponding to one layer of the layered bed, this being achieved through controlled switching of the shutter plate.
